    },
    "body": "Add functional coverage for the `getblockfilter` error raised when a node has a known block header, but the block has never been connected.\n\nThis gap in test coverage was identified by a coverage report generated while exploring BIP 157/158. The branch in `src/rpc/blockchain.cpp` was never executed in the measured tests:\nhttps://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/blob/64cf455b481d36182957bdcfcae7c411a7879897/src/rpc/blockchain.cpp#L3054-L3056\n\nThe existing `getblockfilter` functional test checks unknown block hashes and filter retrieval for active and stale blocks, but doesn’t check a known header whose block has never been connected.\n\nThis change submits only the block header of a newly mined block to a node using `submitheader` and verifies that in this expected state, `getblockfilter` returns error `-5` with `\"Filter not found. Block was not connected to active chain.\"` This adds coverage for the RPC’s distinction between an unknown block and a known block for which no filter has been constructed.\n\n`rpc_getblockfilter.py` passes, and changing the error message makes the new assertion fail as expected.",
